/	/		UPPER to lower case. This allows the programmer
/	/		to disable the case changing at will. Presently
/	/		German disables the case value.
/	0001	GLT	08-Feb-80	Add French German and Dutch translations
/	/		and did amazing things with angle brackets and accented
/	/		characters. By adding the value MAPCON. MAPCON
/	/		defines the first "x" characters that will be mapped
/	/		into lowercase starting with SIXBIT "A". For English
/	/		MAPCON=33 (base 8, 26 base 10) to capitalize A-Z.
/	/		In FORIN systems MAPCON=36 (base 8, 29 base 10) to
/	/		capitalize A-Z plus the three special foreign
/	/		characters. (See OUTSTR for current values).
/	/		French diacritical substitutions:
/	/		"["-L.A.E, "]"-L.G.E
/	/		German diacritical substitutions:
/	/		"["-L.U.A, "\"-L.U.O, "]"-L.U.U
